        "original_id": "2bbd6bf9-3c01-5f26-998e-67bf4d52a8e0",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: James Clark McReynolds, Woodrow Wilson, John Calvin Coolidge Jr.\n- Roles: American lawyer, judge, United States Attorney General, Associate Justice of the United States Supreme Court\n- Organizations: United States Supreme Court\n- Places: Paris\n\nFacts:\n- James Clark McReynolds was born on February 3, 1862.\n- James Clark McReynolds was an American lawyer and judge.\n- James Clark McReynolds served as United States Attorney General under President Woodrow Wilson.\n- James Clark McReynolds served as an Associate Justice of the United States Supreme Court during the presidency of John Calvin Coolidge Jr., who was President of the United States from 1923 to 1929.\n- James Clark McReynolds died in Paris on August 24, 1946.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "567033fe-667e-5872-a2b3-0d9ab50b9e73",
        "text": "James Clark McReynolds (February 3, 1862 – August 24, 1946) was an American lawyer and judge who served as United States Attorney General under President Woodrow Wilson and as an Associate Justice of the United States Supreme Court, he served on the Court, during the presidency of 30th John Calvin Coolidge Jr. President of the United States (1923–29), he died on a trip to Paris.",
